  "question": {
    "text": "The variation of density of a solid cylindrical rod of cross sectional area $\\alpha$ and length $L$ is $\\rho=\\rho_0 \\frac{x^2}{L^2}$, where x is the distance from one end of the rod. The position of its centre of mass from one end $(x=0)$ is\n\n<img width=\"250px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/dUSNHv5M6LqG7wl6kQB6U8VGQXwoj1p1lMfG835gqag.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3fg90",
      "text": "2L/3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dQ6Hp",
      "text": "L/2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PfwGO",
      "text": "L/3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qmprS",
      "text": "3L/4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/gdWqZTpXWzG2dfYqXhBW_LV4IIPJWZw8tzd-CdVHK0g.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\n\n\n$\\rho=\\rho_0 \\frac{x^2}{L^2}$,\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & X=\\frac{\\int x d m}{\\int d m} \\quad d m=\\alpha d x \\rho=\\frac{\\alpha \\rho_0 x^2}{L^2} d x \\\\ & =\\frac{\\rho_0 \\int_0^L x^3 d x}{\\frac{\\rho_0}{L^2} \\int_0^L x^2 d x}=\\frac{\\left[x^4 / 4\\right]_0^L}{\\left[x^3 / 3\\right]_0^L}=3 / 4 L\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
